{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>And you shall make.</b> I have seen scrolls that the sages of Tiberias checked, and fifteen of their elders swore that they examined three times every word and every point, every plene and every defective, and behold it is written with a yod in the word <b>תיעשה</b>, and I have not found thus in the scrolls of Sepharad and France and across the sea. And the ancients interpreted: the added yod alludes to the ten menorahs that Solomon would make. And the principle: if there is a yod there, it is a strange reading, and in derash that it was made of itself. And the reason is that all who saw it were astonished how a man could make it, for behold it is written ויעש מנורת, כן עשה את המנורה (Numbers 8:4), and behold על מחבת בשמן תֵעָשֶׂה מורבכת תביאנה (Leviticus 6:14), and behold מקשה like what is written of the cherubim:" "<b>Its base and its shaft.</b> It is the body of the menorah:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "The Hebrew is somewhat elliptical at 'ובדרש כי נעשית מאליה'; translated hyper-literally. The final clause is truncated in the source text; the comparison to the cherubim is left incomplete as it stands."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:38:28.536260921Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}